  "headline": "WBC's expense to income ratio (ex Notable Items) rose 275 bps (2.75 ppt) to 53.04% in FY25 from 50.29% in FY24. The deterioration was driven by operating expense growth of 9% ($10,944m to $11,916m) significantly outpacing operating income growth of 3% ($21,763m to $22,464m). Expense growth was driven by a $397m rise in staff costs (wage growth, UNITE, investment in bankers), $146m in technology costs (UNITE, amortisation), $359m in investments (UNITE spend), and a $273m Fit for Growth restructuring charge, partially offset by $402m from productivity initiatives. Income growth came from net interest income up 3% (balance sheet growth offset by 1 bp NIM contraction) and non-interest income up 6% (higher card fees, institutional lending fees, markets and net wealth income).",
